WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.866 --> 00:00:02.235 align:start size:78% position:22%
- Hello, I'm Gav.
- I'm Dan.

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:03.569 align:start position:0%
Welcome to
"The Super Slow Show."

00:00:03.602 --> 00:00:06.406 align:start position:0%
Dan, in your quest to look
better in slow motion,

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:09.242 align:start position:0%
you told me you want to
jump through a pane of glass.

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:11.477 align:start size:75% position:25%
I did. I think I would
look bad-ass doing that.

00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:12.545 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Like an action hero.
- Yeah.

00:00:12.578 --> 00:00:15.148 align:start position:0%
And then what happened
yesterday?

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:17.150 align:start size:66% position:34%
I hurt myself
trying to be bad-ass.

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:18.151 size:75% position:38%
And what does that mean?

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:19.786 align:start size:56% position:44%
You have to do it.

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:22.489
<i> ( music playing )</i>

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:32.432 align:start position:0%
So I'm gonna run through
a pane of glass.

00:00:32.465 --> 00:00:34.300
This one is made
of breakaway glass.

00:00:34.333 --> 00:00:36.369
I'm just gonna throw my body
at it full tilt.

00:00:36.402 --> 00:00:37.703
Hopefully,
it won't bounce off.

00:00:37.736 --> 00:00:39.105
And then after that,

00:00:39.138 --> 00:00:40.506 line:0%
why don't we try it
with real glass?

00:00:40.539 --> 00:00:42.742 align:start size:59% position:41% line:0%
Oh, man. I like how
I wanted to do it

00:00:42.775 --> 00:00:44.744 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
and you don't want to do it,
but you have to do it.

00:00:44.777 --> 00:00:47.847 align:start position:0% line:0%
If I find out
that injury's fake,
I'll be livid.

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:49.182 align:start position:0% line:0%
Livid. All right.

00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:50.550 align:start position:0%
( exhales forcefully )

00:00:50.583 --> 00:00:51.717
- ( laughs )
- Okay, ready.

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:53.352 align:start size:91% position:9%
- Is that your game face?
- Yeah.

00:00:53.385 --> 00:00:54.787 align:start position:0%
All right, let's do it.

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:56.189 size:84% position:58%
You're already not bad-ass.

00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:57.624 align:start position:0%
( laughs )

00:01:00.526 --> 00:01:02.462 align:start size:78% position:22%
- How do you feel?
- Uh...

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:05.565
it feels very unnatural to be
wanting to run towards this.

00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:07.400 align:start size:81% position:19%
I can tell,
because you're doing this.

00:01:07.433 --> 00:01:08.401 align:start size:56% position:44%
( exhales )

00:01:08.434 --> 00:01:09.569 align:start size:75% position:25%
- Yeah.
- Pacing around.

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:10.870 align:start position:0%
I'm gonna run through it
like this,

00:01:10.903 --> 00:01:12.605 align:start position:0%
I'm gonna smash it
with my elbow.

00:01:12.638 --> 00:01:13.873 align:start size:16% position:84%
Okay.

00:01:13.906 --> 00:01:16.275
'Cause it would be stupid
to do it like this.

00:01:16.308 --> 00:01:18.878 align:start size:91% position:9%
I think it would look better,
but all right.

00:01:18.911 --> 00:01:20.279 align:start size:88% position:13%
- All right, you ready?
- Yeah.

00:01:20.312 --> 00:01:22.148 align:start size:81% position:19%
- ( inhales )
- Go on, good face.

00:01:22.181 --> 00:01:24.117 align:start position:0%
Oh, bullocks!

00:01:27.286 --> 00:01:29.122 align:start position:0%
May have overshot
the mat slightly.

00:01:30.589 --> 00:01:32.692 align:start size:75% position:25%
That looked so much fun.

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:34.894 align:start size:75% position:25%
Look,
you've left a Gav-shaped
hole in the glass.

00:01:34.927 --> 00:01:36.462
Oh, wow,
it's like a cartoon.

00:01:36.495 --> 00:01:38.231 align:start size:81% position:19%
You're not bleeding out of
your jugular as well,

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:39.232 align:start size:47% position:53%
so that's good.

00:01:39.265 --> 00:01:42.535
<i> ( music playing )</i>

00:01:42.568 --> 00:01:44.871
Dan:
<i> That looks like one of those
 portals in a video game</i>

00:01:44.904 --> 00:01:46.606 align:start size:66% position:34%
where it takes you to
a different dimension
or something.

00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:48.207 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Yeah.
- 'Cause it's like...

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:49.375 align:start position:0%
'Cause of the weird,
sort of, warped-ness

00:01:49.408 --> 00:01:50.576 align:start size:75% position:25%
-<i> of the glass. </i>
-<i> Yeah.</i>

00:01:52.811 --> 00:01:54.747
Gav:
<i> Went to break
 with the knee and elbow.</i>

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:56.182
Dan:
<i> Oh, yeah, that looks good.</i>

00:01:56.215 --> 00:01:58.418
<i> ( Gav imitates shattering )</i>

00:01:59.385 --> 00:02:00.520
Dan:
<i> That's cool.</i>

00:02:00.553 --> 00:02:02.522
Gav:
<i> Oh, that doesn't look bad.</i>

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:04.524
Dan:
<i> Straight through.
 You look bad-ass for sure.</i>

00:02:04.557 --> 00:02:06.225
Gav:
<i> Oh, the glass
 looks cool, though.</i>

00:02:06.258 --> 00:02:08.828
Dan:
<i> You made some spin
 quite high up there.</i>

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:19.839
Gav:
<i> If that was real glass,
 I'd be cut to ribbons.</i>

00:02:19.872 --> 00:02:21.875
Dan:
<i> You'd be in pieces right now.</i>

00:02:29.848 --> 00:02:34.253
Gav:
<i> Look at the incredibly
 unglamorous landing.</i>

00:02:34.286 --> 00:02:35.521
<i> ( both laugh )</i>

00:02:35.554 --> 00:02:37.757
<i> On my head, legs spread.</i>

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:40.526
Dan:
<i> You ended up half way along
 the mat when you landed,</i>

00:02:40.559 --> 00:02:42.495
<i> and then you almost went
 off the edge.</i>

00:02:42.528 --> 00:02:44.230 line:0%
That is
not glamorous there.

00:02:44.263 --> 00:02:45.565 align:start size:91% position:9% line:0%
- No.
- Look how your legs are.

00:02:45.598 --> 00:02:47.233 align:start position:0% line:0%
I've never seen Stallone
land like that.

00:02:47.266 --> 00:02:48.935 line:0%
You went from
looking bad-ass

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:50.636
-<i> to completely
 not bad-ass... </i>
-<i> ( both laugh )</i>

00:02:50.669 --> 00:02:51.804
<i> in about two meters.</i>

00:02:51.837 --> 00:02:54.273 align:start position:0%
More bad-ass than you
in the background.

00:02:54.306 --> 00:02:55.675 align:start size:56% position:44%
( mocking babble )

00:02:57.843 --> 00:02:59.712 align:start size:47% position:53%
So you've done
the fake glass.

00:02:59.745 --> 00:03:01.581 align:start size:91% position:9%
- Yes.
- How was that? All right?

00:03:01.614 --> 00:03:03.716 align:start position:0%
Yeah, felt it,
but it was fine. Yep.

00:03:03.749 --> 00:03:06.252 align:start size:72% position:28%
Now for the real thing.
Yeah.

00:03:06.285 --> 00:03:08.387 align:start position:0%
Yeah, the other one
I was sort of nervous
to even touch

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:11.324 size:78% position:39%
because it was breakaway.
This one's just glass.

00:03:11.357 --> 00:03:12.625 align:start size:66% position:34%
This is solid. It's--

00:03:12.658 --> 00:03:13.993 size:88% position:56%
It's tempered glass as well.

00:03:14.026 --> 00:03:15.661 align:start size:81% position:19%
So it's not like the glass
where it gets sharp.

00:03:15.694 --> 00:03:16.762 align:start size:69% position:31%
It's the safety glass.

00:03:16.795 --> 00:03:18.531 align:start size:75% position:25%
So hopefully
you should be all right.

00:03:18.564 --> 00:03:21.601
That all depends on if
our little mechanism works.

00:03:21.634 --> 00:03:24.237 align:start size:56% position:44%
I'll just take you
through it.

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:26.739 align:start position:0%
So, we've wired up
a small detonator.

00:03:26.772 --> 00:03:28.874 align:start position:0%
Just before you go through it,
I'll detonate it

00:03:28.907 --> 00:03:30.810 align:start size:81% position:19%
and smash the glass
just before you get to it.

00:03:30.843 --> 00:03:34.447 align:start position:0%
So if you're too early,
the shot doesn't look as good.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:36.015 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Yeah.
- If you're too late,

00:03:36.048 --> 00:03:38.417
- You just into the glass.
- I run into sheet glass

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:40.019 align:start size:94% position:6%
- and bounce off, probably.
- Pretty much.

00:03:40.052 --> 00:03:42.689 align:start size:88% position:13%
And then I detonate it,
and then it just falls down.

00:03:43.889 --> 00:03:46.592
<i> ( music playing )</i>

00:03:46.625 --> 00:03:47.760 align:start size:78% position:22%
I'm ready on the trigger.

00:03:47.793 --> 00:03:49.528 align:start size:63% position:38%
Are you ready to run
through real glass?

00:03:49.561 --> 00:03:51.497
I think my motivation
on this one

00:03:51.530 --> 00:03:53.532
is I'm in a skyscraper

00:03:53.565 --> 00:03:54.967
and it's gonna blow up.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:57.303
- I got to get out.
- Okay. Excellent.

00:03:57.336 --> 00:03:59.305 align:start position:0%
Here we go.

00:03:59.338 --> 00:04:00.707
- ( exhales )
- I'm ready.

00:04:03.375 --> 00:04:06.679 align:start position:0%
( groans, laughs )

00:04:08.781 --> 00:04:11.851 align:start size:44% position:56%
Oh!

00:04:11.884 --> 00:04:13.653 align:start size:56% position:44%
Oh, my God!

00:04:13.686 --> 00:04:14.820 align:start size:69% position:31%
- I'm fine.
- Oh.

00:04:14.853 --> 00:04:16.322 align:start position:0% line:0%
Man:
It blew. It didn't
break the glass.

00:04:16.355 --> 00:04:17.523 line:0%
You good, dude?
Your elbow okay?

00:04:17.556 --> 00:04:18.958 align:start size:69% position:31%
- Yeah.
- Oh, Jesus.

00:04:22.094 --> 00:04:26.732
- ( muttering )
- ( laughs )

00:04:26.765 --> 00:04:28.434 align:start size:25% position:75%
Oh!

00:04:28.467 --> 00:04:30.936 align:start size:59% position:41%
I promise I pressed
the trigger.

00:04:30.969 --> 00:04:33.339 align:start size:69% position:31%
- I promise.
- Oh.

00:04:33.372 --> 00:04:34.674 align:start size:69% position:31%
I did not expect that.

00:04:34.707 --> 00:04:36.342 align:start size:69% position:31% line:0%
- You okay?
- Yeah.

00:04:37.843 --> 00:04:41.647 align:start size:59% position:41% line:0%
( laughs )
That was hilarious!

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:43.082 align:start size:81% position:19% line:0%
I'm so glad that happened.

00:04:43.115 --> 00:04:44.950
<i> ( music playing )</i>

00:04:44.983 --> 00:04:46.819
Gav:
<i> I was so naive and innocent.</i>

00:04:46.852 --> 00:04:48.688
<i> I thought I'd be through.</i>

00:04:48.721 --> 00:04:51.457
<i> Well, I felt like,
 if I curled up more,</i>

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:53.092 line:0%
I would definitely
go through

00:04:53.125 --> 00:04:55.995 line:0%
'cause I'm focusing more energy
into a smaller area.

00:04:56.028 --> 00:04:57.363 line:0%
That was the theory.

00:05:00.632 --> 00:05:02.702
-<i> Oh! </i>
-<i> Oh!</i>

00:05:02.735 --> 00:05:05.538
Dan:<i> That's such
 a heavy impact.</i>

00:05:05.571 --> 00:05:08.708
<i> Because it's so clear,</i>

00:05:08.741 --> 00:05:11.644
<i> it looks like you just
 got stopped by nothing.</i>

00:05:21.820 --> 00:05:24.957
<i> Look at me laughing
 in the background.</i>

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:27.460
-<i> Look at that! </i>
-<i> What is that?</i>

00:05:27.493 --> 00:05:30.763 align:start size:78% position:22%
<i> ( slow motion laughing )</i>

00:05:34.433 --> 00:05:35.668 align:start size:69% position:31%
Well, how'd that feel?

00:05:35.701 --> 00:05:38.537 size:84% position:42%
It didn't feel magnificent.

00:05:38.570 --> 00:05:39.839 align:start size:81% position:19%
- No?
- Didn't feel great.

00:05:39.872 --> 00:05:41.941 align:start position:0%
See, now I'm at a disadvantage
because I knew

00:05:41.974 --> 00:05:44.043 align:start position:0%
there was the possibility
it wouldn't break,

00:05:44.076 --> 00:05:46.579
- Yeah.
- but now I know what it feels
like when it doesn't break.

00:05:46.612 --> 00:05:48.514 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Oh, yeah.
- So now am I gonna have

00:05:48.547 --> 00:05:50.683 align:start position:0%
the same level of beans
running towards it?

00:05:50.716 --> 00:05:52.017 align:start size:56% position:44%
Well, technically,

00:05:52.050 --> 00:05:53.519 align:start size:59% position:41%
you're not the one
breaking the glass.

00:05:53.552 --> 00:05:54.553 align:start size:78% position:22%
So you don't even need...

00:05:54.586 --> 00:05:55.688
Well, you can say that again.

00:05:55.721 --> 00:05:57.022
- Bloody hell.
- ( laughs )

00:05:57.055 --> 00:05:58.858 align:start position:0%
All right.

00:05:58.891 --> 00:06:00.460
- You ready?
- Here we go.

00:06:03.529 --> 00:06:05.598 align:start size:19% position:81%
Oh-ho!

00:06:05.631 --> 00:06:07.767
- Man: Freeze!
- You made it!

00:06:13.839 --> 00:06:15.775 align:start position:0%
Keep your eyes closed.

00:06:18.610 --> 00:06:19.779 align:start size:56% position:44%
All right,
you got a little--

00:06:19.812 --> 00:06:22.081
couple of little nicks in you,

00:06:22.114 --> 00:06:23.582 align:start position:0%
but nothing serious.

00:06:23.615 --> 00:06:26.085
<i> ( music playing )</i>

00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:29.922
Gav:
<i> Oh, there's the charge going.</i>

00:06:29.955 --> 00:06:31.524
Dan:
<i> That's a beefier charge,
 for sure.</i>

00:06:31.557 --> 00:06:32.925
Gav:
<i> It flew out past me.</i>

00:06:32.958 --> 00:06:34.560 align:start size:63% position:38% line:0%
You really tucked up
this time.

00:06:34.593 --> 00:06:35.861 line:0%
- ( laughs )
- Didn't you?

00:06:35.894 --> 00:06:37.530 line:0%
I really wanted to go through.

00:06:37.563 --> 00:06:38.831 align:start size:9% position:91% line:0%
Oh.

00:06:40.966 --> 00:06:42.568
Gav:
<i> It's like I'm just wearing</i>

00:06:42.601 --> 00:06:44.503
<i> a glass suit coming through.</i>

00:06:44.536 --> 00:06:46.772
Dan:
<i> It does look super cool
 'cause it-- like,</i>

00:06:46.805 --> 00:06:49.842
<i> the glass follows
 your shape, doesn't it?</i>

00:06:52.945 --> 00:06:54.547 line:0%
Gav:
<i> Oh, it just looks awful,</i>

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:56.081 line:0%
<i> just landing on
 a load of real glass.</i>

00:06:56.114 --> 00:06:57.683 line:0%
Dan:
<i> It's amazing that
 that is real glass.</i>

00:06:57.716 --> 00:06:58.951 line:0%
<i> Because it's safety glass,
 though,</i>

00:06:58.984 --> 00:07:01.520 line:0%
<i> it's, like, all you've got
 is a tiny little cut.</i>

00:07:01.553 --> 00:07:03.889 line:0%
Gav:
<i> I couldn't really feel
 the cuts on my face and neck.</i>

00:07:03.922 --> 00:07:05.892 line:0%
<i> I felt them on
 my finger more.</i>

00:07:19.705 --> 00:07:21.207
<i> Yeah, you could never do that
 through non-tempered glass.</i>

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:22.441
Dan:<i> No.</i>

00:07:22.475 --> 00:07:24.210
<i> You got the effect
 that we were after, though,</i>

00:07:24.243 --> 00:07:26.813
<i> where it, like,
 follows your body around.</i>

00:07:31.517 --> 00:07:32.852 align:start position:0%
Hopefully you enjoyed
that video.

